# Facebook posts — Mejor Vida Insurance

When **creating**, **previewing**, or **publishing** Facebook posts for this project:

1. **Read and apply** the full standard in **`facebook-post-rules.md`** at the repository root.

2. **Non‑negotiables** (see that file for detail):
   - **No blog URL in the main caption** — link only in the **first follow-up comment** (and/or automation), not in the primary post text.
   - **Dual CTA** when possible: **INFO** (article/education) and **REVISAR** (review/help) + option to **DM** instead of commenting.
   - **Hook** must not read like a newsletter, report title, or “en este artículo…” blog opener.
   - Tone: human, simple Spanish, families — not agents or regulators.
   - **Compliance:** no guarantees on coverage, pricing, or outcomes; educational and trust-building only.

3. **Weekly post deliverables** should include: main caption, shorter alternate, first comment with URL, image concept/prompt, ManyChat keywords, optional pinned comment — as specified in `facebook-post-rules.md`.

4. **`facebook-posting/main.py`** builds a **`FacebookPostPackage`**: main caption has **no** URL; **`first_comment`** links to **mejorvidainsurance.com** (not the blog — articles via INFO/REVISAR). JSON export: **`FB/post-package.json`**. After publish, **`publish_post_package`** POSTs `post_id` + `first_comment` to the Make.com webhook (10 min delay in Make). Use **`--no-first-comment`** to skip.
